      "parents": [],
      "description": "One row per source file landed by download_aemo.py, read from csv_raw_archive_log.parquet. Every engine reads the SAME parquet file, which is what makes the fact models' file-selection logic identical across engines.",
      "differences": [
        "A view on DuckDB, in its in-memory catalog: the OneLake Iceberg catalog has no `CREATE VIEW`. The other engines rebuild a table every run.",
        "Reading the parquet log: `read_parquet()` on DuckDB and Polars; a `USING parquet` temp view on Spark (for `parquet.`path``, OneLake answers the catalog lookup with 400); a Hive external table on Trino."
      ]
    },
